 ### LUE (Uncertainty-aware Regularization Loss)
-A regularization loss that models ray uncertainty to improve rendering reliability and reduce artifacts in few-shot settings, applied to both original rays ($r$) and flipped rays ($r'$) [S3]. Apply LUE to both the original ray $r$ and the flipped ray $r'$ during optimization [S3]. With LUE, NLL drops to 2.56 (vs 4.88 without LUE or Lemp.), PSNR reaches 19.55, SSIM 0.767, LPIPS 0.180, and Average Error 0.101 on Realistic Synthetic 360◦ [S3]. Unlike MixNeRF which uses a mixture-of-distributions model, LUE consistently produces more reliable outputs with lower Negative Log-Likelihood (NLL). Naively applying Lemp. (emptiness loss) degrades performance below MixNeRF, whereas LUE improves it [S3].
